            <ArticleTitle>Failed disk syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>86-94</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Over half the patients in most pain clinics in the United States are seeking relief from the &quot;failed disk syndrome.&quot; Careful initial diagnostic evaluation and aggressive nonoperative therapy are essential to avoid poor results. Causes of continued pain after disk surgery include original pain syndromes not due to a disk, inadequate surgery, development of arthritis, additional disk disorders and nerve root fibrosis. Treatment demands precise diagnosis. Diagnostic injections and nerve blocks are helpful when other techniques fail.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
